  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Buka Electricity Grid Solar Upgrade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A NZ$17 million contribution to an up to 10MW solar plant, battery system and grid extension for Buka Island in Bougainville which will reduce diesel usage by over 90%. The project is partly funded by Australian Government Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT). New Zealand contributions will also support initial operations and maintenance upon construction completion.</narrative>
  </description>
